# Array push and pop performance

Measures 5,000,000 push/pop pairs on one array that holds a single element, so
the workload measures the end operations themselves: an append that claims the
free slot after the last element and a removal that moves the element out of
it. Neither operation moves the other elements, so a per-operation regression
such as an extra clone or a type lookup shows up directly. Only the final total
is printed so benchmark output does not dominate execution.

>>> source
let values: int[] = []
let total: int = 0
for (iteration in 0..5000000) {
    values->push(iteration)
    let removed = values->pop()
    if (removed != null) {
        total = total + removed
    }
}
print(total)
